Basic Batch Scripting Command and How they work


1. echo 
   -   shows text on the screen.Its like Print Command.
  Example : echo hello!
  How it work :
  Display Hello! to the user.  

2. @echo off
    - Hide command so the screen looks clean.
     How it Work:
     Prevents CMD from showing each command before running it.

3. pause
    - Waits until the user presses a key to continue.
    How it Work:
    Pauses the execution of the script and displays "Press any key to continue..."until the user presses a key.

4. cls
    - Clear the CMD screen.
    How it work:
    Removes all current text on the screen.

5. rem / :::
    - Comment or note for human.
    How it work:
    CMD ignore this line, allowing you to add explanations or notes in your script. 

6. start 
    - Opens a program or file in a new window.
     Example : start notepad.exe
     how it work;
     Launches the chosen application.

7. dir
    - Shows the files and folders in the current directory.
    how it work:
    Text version of opening a folder in windows explorer, Lists all files .

8. cd
    - Change directory to different folder.
    Example : cd C:\Users\username\documents
    how it Work:
    Changes the current working directory to the specified path.

 9. mkdir
    - Creates a new Directory.
    Example : mkdir NewFolder
    How it work;
    Creates a new folder named "NewFolder" in the current directory.Same as creating a folder in windows explorer.

10. rmdir
    -Removes a directory.
    Example : rmdir OldFolder
    How it Work:
    Deletes the specific folder named "OldFolder" from the current directory. Note that the folder must be empty to be removed.  

11. del
   - Deletes one or more files.
   Example : del file.text
   How it work :
   Removes the specified file from the current directory. You can also use wildcards to delete multiple files at once.

12. copy 
    -Copies files from one location to another.
    Example : copy file.text D:\Backup\
    How it work:
    Copies the specific file to the specified destination folder. If the destination folder does not exist, it will prompt to create it.

13. copy con
   - Creates a new file and allows you to input text directly into it.
   Example : copy con file.text
   How it Work:
   Creates a new file named 'File.text' and allow you to type text into it. press Ctrl+Z to save and exit.

14. move
    - Moves files from one location to another.
    Example : move file.text D:\Backup\
    How it work:
    Transfers the specific file to the specified destination folder.